title The seed published, and four doors named
prompt Keaton: publish the seed now even mid-lap because the readme is significantly better; and the GitHub descriptions for the personal fields and the public seeds should each say plainly which they are, at the maximum length, as Bhakta invitations -- you can update all.
rota none -- a publish and an outward-facing edit on Keaton's explicit word; the Air row was read this sitting at 20260908.143400.
think The force-push is custody gate %1 -- the publisher's own header says an autonomous agent stops there and never crosses. Keaton's word is what opens it, so the gate was honoured rather than bypassed: the bare form ran first, proving the projection, and only then the push.
obs THE SEED PUBLISHED CLEAN: 8,187 files, parentless root, unsigned by design, authored by the anonymous grain-ww identity. IDENT_CLEAN and NO_PERSONAL both passed and SOW_WITNESS_GREEN stood before either door was touched. Both doors force-updated from ONE commit in one run, which is what keeps two seeds from becoming two truths.
obs THE FRONT DOOR IS THE REASON THIS PUBLISH WAS WORTH INTERRUPTING FOR. The readme went into Bhakta an hour earlier and grades 93 where it stood lower; a seed carrying a warmer front door reaches a newcomer that the elder one turned away.
obs THE TWO PERSONAL FIELDS WERE PUBLIC AND SAID NOTHING ABOUT BEING PERSONAL. xykj61 and debrided both read `private=false` and carried the same 112-character line as each other, describing the project rather than the repository. A stranger landing there met one hand's sessions, ledgers and reds with no warning about what kind of place it was.
obs AND THE TWO SEEDS SAID `crashed-meteor`, FOURTEEN CHARACTERS. The one word that names the phase and nothing that names the offer. A public template whose description is an internal code word is a door with no sign.
obs SO EACH PAIR NOW SAYS WHICH IT IS, AT LENGTH, IN THE REGISTER THE READMES NOW USE. The fields name themselves personal by nature and point at the public template; the seeds name themselves a public template, say what stays on your machine, and invite a first hour. 339 and 333 characters against GitHub's 350.
obs I WROTE 359 FIRST AND MEASURED BEFORE PUSHING, WHICH IS THE HABIT RATHER THAN THE LUCK. Nine over the ceiling would have been truncated mid-sentence at the one place a reader looks first. Trimmed to 339 by hand, asserted under the limit in the same breath, then applied and read back from GitHub rather than assumed.
loom publish files=8187 parents=0 signed=N commit=1162fb15 doors=2 ident=CLEAN personal=NONE
loom descriptions field_chars=339 seed_chars=333 limit=350 first_draft=359 repos_updated=4 verified=4
